From: tukken-comcast <tony_ukken2@comcast.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cache: log negative upstream DNS replies for field diagnostics

Log NXDOMAIN/NODATA and SERVFAIL/REFUSED (and other error rcode) replies from
upstream servers even when log-queries is disabled, so transient DNS resolution
failures in the field can be diagnosed without the full query-logging flood.

This reuses the existing log_query() path: the early !log-queries return is
skipped only for replies carrying F_UPSTREAM together with F_NEG or F_RCODE.
Cached and locally-generated negatives lack F_UPSTREAM and are not logged, so
repeat lookups do not flood the log. The responding upstream server address is
not included (log_query has no access to it at this point).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream field diagnostics]
Signed-off-by: tukken-comcast <tony_ukken2@comcast.com>
---
diff --git a/src/cache.c b/src/cache.c
index 0eacec9..1f6c44d 100644
--- a/src/cache.c
+++ b/src/cache.c
@@ -2100,7 +2100,11 @@ void log_query(unsigned int flags, char *name, union all_addr *addr, char *arg,
   char *gap = " ";
   char portstring[7]; /* space for #<portnum> */
   
-  if (!option_bool(OPT_LOG))
+  /* Log negative upstream replies (NXDOMAIN/NODATA and SERVFAIL/REFUSED etc.)
+     even when query logging is disabled, to diagnose transient field failures.
+     Cached and locally-generated negatives lack F_UPSTREAM, so are not logged. */
+  if (!option_bool(OPT_LOG) &&
+      !((flags & F_UPSTREAM) && (flags & (F_NEG | F_RCODE))))
     return;
 
   /* build query type string if requested */
